    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d423">

                <pb facs="0575" n="565" xml:id="pg565"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Joint Chiefs of Staff to the Commanding General,
                        United States Forces, China Theater</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wedemeyer</hi>)<anchor n="58a" xml:id="d423-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-09-18">18 September 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Warx 66085. It is U. S. policy to assist the Chinese Government in the
                    establishment of essential Chinese troops in liberated areas, particularly
                    Manchuria, as rapidly as practicable.</p>
                <p>Movement of Chinese Forces will be executed, in so far as practicable, in general
                    conformity with the schedule indicated in Wedemeyer’s CFBX 8412 dated 17
                    September 1945,<anchor n="59" xml:id="d423-f2"/> utilizing for this purpose
                    shipping now under your control. To effect this movement, maximum use will be
                    made of shipping unsuitable for trans-Pacific use.</p>
                <p>Request you report to the Joint Chiefs of Staff, with information copy to
                    CinCAFPac, the action you take to move Chinese Forces in compliance with this
                    directive.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d423-f1" n="58a" type="source" xml:id="d423-f1-content">
                <p>Sent also to Fleet Admiral Nimitz.</p>
            </note>
